2026-11-22 09:59:29 - Agent_20261122095505 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed both queries in the group; both point to the same root weakness in src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/periodic_update.py. Confirmed two true positives: (1) line ~336 — `_request_context()` intentionally yields `ssl._create_unverified_context()`, disabling TLS certificate verification; (2) line 353 — that unverified context is passed to `urlopen()` when fetching PyPI JSON metadata, allowing a MITM to inject/spoof release-date metadata that influences wheel version selection. No sanitizers, pinning, or post-fetch integrity checks were found. The actual wheel download happens via a separate `pip download` subprocess, which bounds impact to metadata tampering rather than direct code execution.
